# Threat-intel blocklist snapshot, hosts format: `<ip> <hostname>` per line.
#
# Hosts format is the syntax of /etc/hosts; feeds publish in it so the file can
# be dropped onto a machine or a Pi-hole to sinkhole every listed domain to
# 0.0.0.0. The analyzer uses only the hostname column.
#
# In production this would be a live feed such as the URLhaus hosts list
# (https://urlhaus.abuse.ch/). It is committed here as a pinned, offline
# excerpt so the lab is deterministic (the e2e gate asserts exact verdicts) and
# needs no network access. Swap in a fresh download and the analyzer is
# unchanged.
#
# Note what is NOT listed: updates.goodvendor.lab. The vendor's update check
# must come out `clean` to show the report covers the app's full footprint.

# --- seeded lab malware infrastructure ---
0.0.0.0 cdn-metrics.tracklab.lab
0.0.0.0 telemetry.adnexus.lab
0.0.0.0 pin.evil-c2.lab

# --- placeholder feed excerpt: .invalid is a reserved TLD that never resolves,
#     standing in for the thousands of real entries a production feed carries ---
0.0.0.0 login-secure-update.invalid
0.0.0.0 cdn-cache-node-7.invalid
0.0.0.0 analytics-collector.invalid
